        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0142" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg94"/>

                <head>No. 67.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 19, 1877</date>.
                        (Received May 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 221.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have bad the honor to receive your
                    instruction, No. 92, in regard to services rendered by Captain Stewart, of the
                    imperial Chinese gunboat Sin Ching, to the American ship Enoch Train.</p>
                <p>I have communicated with the foreign office as instructed, and transmit to you
                    herewith a copy of my note and of the response which I have received.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEOEGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d67-a1.xml" xpointer="d67-a1"/>
